In Warp, filters are used to define the processing pipeline for a request. They are used to process the request and produce a response. Filters can be combined to create more complex pipelines.

`warp::filters::query` provides a pre-defined filter, `query()`, which is used to extract query parameters from the incoming request. This filter automatically extracts all the query parameters and returns a `HashMap<String, String>`.

